Keep whois reply lines whole.
Each piece read by fgets was cut at its first CR or LF and given a new
LF, so text after a CR in the middle of a line was dropped, and a line
longer than the 2046-byte buffer was broken into 2046-byte lines, with
an extra empty line when the line end came in a piece of its own (a
line of exactly 2046 bytes, or 2046 bytes and CR LF). Keep the pieces
of a long line together, replace only the line's own LF or CR LF with
LF, even when the CR ends one piece and the LF starts the next, look
for the "domain:" and "whois:" prefixes only at the start of a line,
and end an unterminated last line once. A piece cut short by a NUL
byte still ends the line, as before.

